    "test_cases": [
      "every port of the frozen multi-process boundary is disposed exactly once",
      "The numerator sums the counted exchanges from the selected solved inventory; demonstration totals are regression fixtures, not constraints on measured input.",
      "a boundary frozen against another model graph is refused",
      "an undecided or undeclared required item refuses the full result instead of returning a smaller one",
      "a counted greenhouse gas other than CO2 for this good is refused rather than summed in",
      "a declared end use of further_rolling_or_forging refuses the result instead of reporting the quantity as crude steel"
    ],
    "validation_rules": {
      "limitations": [
        "direct emissions only; Annex II makes electricity indirect emissions non-attributable for this good (ST-12)",
        "no precursor is counted, because none of the eight boundary-crossing inputs of this model is a good of Annex I once the 7204 scrap exclusion of ST-14 and the in-house sinter and hot metal of ST-15 are read (modeling gap MG-S08 covers the purchased-precursor strand that is absent by design)",
        "the route's secondary gases are netted inside the boundary and all of their carbon is charged to the numerator, so the result is a conservative upper bound for an installation that sells gas out (modeling gap MG-S11)",
        "flue gas cleaning reagents and the carbonate they decompose are an open coverage item rather than a counted or excluded exchange (modeling gap MG-S09)"
      ]
    }
